  "format": "{name, kind, …}, the other fields by kind. reveal {input, code, output}: every hidden character (general category Cc, Cf, Cs, Co, Cn, Zl or Zp, or Default_Ignorable_Code_Point) shown as ⟨U+XXXX⟩, except TAB and LF, and in prose (code false) also ZWJ U+200D and the presentation selectors U+FE0E and U+FE0F. revealLine {input, output}: prose, with TAB and LF revealed too. copyText {input, output}: what a code block's Copy puts on the clipboard: trailing whitespace dropped, then revealed as code. linkTitle {label, url, output}: a link's title, \"<label> · <host>\" without www., with \" ⚠\uFE0E non-ASCII host\" for a non-ASCII or punycode host; the url itself when it has no host. stepTitle {url, output}: \"Open <host>\" for an http(s) URL with a host, else null. replyWire {choice, words, output}: the reply text sent for a choice, with the trimmed words after \" · \". replyParse {text, choices, index, words}: which choice a reply text picked (index, or null) and its words (or null); labels are tried longest first. counter {count, limit, shows, text, over}: the length counter: shown past 80 % of the limit, digits grouped by U+202F, and the trim line over the limit (else null). deepLink {url, id}: the ask id a hook:// (or legacy relay://) URL opens, lowercased, or null for anything else (hook://show included). sourceKey {url, context, output}: the namespace for a Pond's per-source state on a device. Hidden characters in inputs and outputs are written as JSON \\u escapes.",
